{"content":[{"c":["MALACHI (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Author of the last book of the OT (",{"href":"?bref=Mal.1.1","r":"Mal.1.1","rawR":"Mal.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mal.1.1","value":"Mal.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mal 1:1"},"). The prophet Malachi lived about 500–460 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},". His name means “my angel” or “my messenger” and is so translated in ",{"href":"?bref=Mal.3.1","r":"Mal.3.1","rawR":"Mal.3.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mal.3.1","value":"Mal.3.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Malachi 3:1"}," and elsewhere. Apart from the book that bears his name, nothing else is known about him from the Bible. In the apocryphal book of ",{"href":"?bref=2Esd.1.40","r":"2Esd.1.40","rawR":"2Esd.1.40","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Esd.1.40","value":"2Esd.1.40"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Esdras 1:40"}," he is identified as “Malachi, who is also called a messenger of the Lord.” Rabbinic tradition suggests that Malachi may be another name for Ezra the scribe, although there is no supporting evidence for this identification."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=MalachiBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"MalachiBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"MalachiBookof_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Malachi, Book of"},"; ",{"href":"?item=ProphetProphetess_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"ProphetProphetess_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"ProphetProphetess_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Prophet, Prophetess"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"MalachiPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Mal 1:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mal.1.1","rawQueryValue":"Mal.1.1","sourceRefExact":"Mal.1.1"},{"anchorText":"Malachi 3:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mal.3.1","rawQueryValue":"Mal.3.1","sourceRefExact":"Mal.3.1"},{"anchorText":"2 Esdras 1:40","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Esd.1.40","rawQueryValue":"2Esd.1.40","sourceRefExact":"2Esd.1.40"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"884bb23a725da599774613b9d9bf41dc4350495e63f1b7a6a496ec2ffdd1677a","sourceItemName":"MalachiPerson","sourceItemOrder":83,"sourceMember":"Articles/M.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"MalachiPerson","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Malachi (Person)","title":"Malachi (Person)","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}